Q: What is CQRS?
	CQRS stands for Command Query Responsibility Segregation. IT is an architectural pattern that separates read operations (Queries) from write operations (Commands).

	Why use CQRS?
		Read and write workloads can be scaled independently.
		Read model can be optimized for queries.
		Complex domains can benefit from separate models.
		Can work well with event-driven architecture.

	Disadvantage
		More complexity.
		Potential eventual consistency.
		More infrastructure and synchronization logic.

	Instead of using the same model for both reading and updating data:
		Command Side → Handles Create, Update, Delete operations.
		Query Side → Handles Read operations.

		Business logic becomes easier to maintain.
			CustomerCommandService
			CustomerQueryService

		4. Supports Event-Driven Architecture
			Often used with:
				Kafka
				RabbitMQ
