4. What is Strategy Design Pattern?
	The Strategy Pattern is used when you have multiple ways (algorithms/behaviors) to perform the same task and
	want to choose between them at runtime.
	Without Strategy:
		if(paymentType.equals("CARD")) {}
		else if(paymentType.equals("UPI")) {}
		else if(paymentType.equals("NET_BANKING")) {}

	With Strategy:
	interface PaymentStrategy {
		void pay();
	}

	CardPaymentStrategy
	UpiPaymentStrategy
	NetBankingStrategy

	Benefits:
		Open/Closed Principle
		Easily extensible
		Removes large if-else blocks
