Q: What is Serialization?
	Serialization converts an object into a byte stream so it can be:
		Stored
		Transferred over network (Json / XML)
		Cached

	Deserialization
		Converting byte stream back into object.

	What is serialVersionUID ?
		serialVersionUID is a unique version identifier used during serialization.
		private static final long serialVersionUID = 1L;

	How can we achieve Serialization in Java?
        1. Implement java.io.Serializable interface
        2. Mark fields as transient if they should not be serialized
        3. Optionally define a serialVersionUID for version control
