Q: What are ACID Properties?
	ACID guarantees reliable database transactions. It ensures transactions are reliable, consistent, isolated, and durable.
	A - Atomicity
		Atomicity ensures that all operations in a transaction succeed together or the entire transaction is rolled back. No partial updates remain.
		Debit Account / Credit Account			// Both succeed or rollback.
	C - Consistency
		Database remains in a valid state. A transaction must move the database from one valid state to another valid state.		// Balance, inventory cannot become negative.
	I - Isolation
		Isolation ensures that concurrent transactions do not affect each other and execute as if they were running independently.		// Two users updating same account.
	D - Durability
		Durability guarantees that once a transaction is committed, its changes are permanently saved and will survive crashes or system failures.		// System crash after commit
