Q: @Transactional exists in both Spring and Jakarta. What is the difference?
	There are two annotations:
	1. Spring @Transactional (Highly recommended)
		org.springframework.transaction.annotation.Transactional
		Example:
			@Transactional(
				propagation = Propagation.REQUIRES_NEW,
				isolation = Isolation.REPEATABLE_READ,
				rollbackFor = Exception.class
			)
			public void process() {
			}
		Features :
			Supports advanced transaction configuration:
				Propagation
				Isolation Level
				Timeout
				Read Only
				rollbackFor
				noRollbackFor

	2. Jakarta @Transactional
		jakarta.transaction.Transactional
		Part of Jakarta EE (formerly Java EE).
		Example:
			@Transactional
			public void process() {
			}

		Features: But provides fewer customization options than Spring's version.
			TxType.REQUIRED
			TxType.REQUIRES_NEW
			TxType.MANDATORY

