Q: I have static block, variable, and method ? What will be execution flow ?
    Execution flow:
        1. Static variables are initialized first.
        2. Static blocks are executed in the order they appear in the class.
        3. Instance variables are initialized when an object is created.
        4. Instance blocks are executed in the order they appear in the class when an object is created.
        5. Constructors are executed after instance blocks when an object is created.
        6. Methods are executed when they are called.

    Example:
        public class Example {
            static int staticVar = initializeStaticVar();
            static {
                System.out.println("Static block executed");
            }
            int instanceVar = initializeInstanceVar();
            {
                System.out.println("Instance block executed");
            }
            public Example() {
                System.out.println("Constructor executed");
            }
            static int initializeStaticVar() {
                System.out.println("Static variable initialized");
                return 1;
            }
            int initializeInstanceVar() {
                System.out.println("Instance variable initialized");
                return 2;
            }
            public static void main(String[] args) {
                new Example();
            }
        }

    Output:
        Static variable initialized
        Static block executed
        Instance variable initialized
        Instance block executed
        Constructor executed
